WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.612
Given an instruction, how should the robot act—and how will the world respond?

2
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:18.662
We introduce UNITAS: A 3D-Native World-Action Model for Embodied Manipulation.

3
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:26.540
Calibrated RGB-D observations bring the scene into a shared three-dimensional space.

4
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:35.068
Given an observation and an instruction, we first predict how the gripper should move.

5
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.280
That predicted motion conditions how the rest of the scene will change.

6
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.132
From articulated motion, to close contact with everyday objects.

7
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.948
Across diverse tasks and simulated environments.

8
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:16.532
UNITAS. Unifying observation, action, and world dynamics in one physical space.

